From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Niklas Sheth <hi@niklassheth.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 22:48:21 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] rust: types: Make Owned<T> Unpin for any T

Owned<T> holds T through a pointer, like KBox<T>, so it is Unpin for any T.
Without this, Owned<Page> (Page now wraps Opaque) is !Unpin and so is any
structure holding one, which v7.3's Mutex guards cannot mutably deref.

Signed-off-by: Niklas Sheth <hi@niklassheth.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RvQieG9SGoR3ZeSdSguHnB
---
 rust/kernel/types.rs | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/rust/kernel/types.rs b/rust/kernel/types.rs
index 2c0d10cf71ce..65f45dc66050 100644
--- a/rust/kernel/types.rs
+++ b/rust/kernel/types.rs
@@ -479,6 +479,9 @@ pub struct Owned<T: Ownable> {
     _p: PhantomData<T>,
 }
 
+// `Owned<T>` owns `T` through a pointer, like `KBox<T>`: moving it never moves the `T`.
+impl<T: Ownable> Unpin for Owned<T> {}
+
 // SAFETY: It is safe to send `Owned<T>` to another thread when the underlying `T` is `Send` because
 // it effectively means sharing `&mut T` (which is safe because `T` is `Send`).
 unsafe impl<T: Ownable + Send> Send for Owned<T> {}
